# Cursor Rules for The A&M Internationals

## Project Overview
Enterprise B2B website for The A&M Internationals, specializing in Oracle EPM Cloud, Financial Transformation, and Enterprise AI & Automations.

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19
- Language: TypeScript 5
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4, Lucide React icons
- Internationalization: Intlayer / next-intlayer (Bilingual English & Arabic)
- Animation: GSAP, Lenis Smooth Scroll, AOS
- Backend / Services: Firebase (v12), Nodemailer, AWS S3 Client

## Verification & Commands
- Dev Server: `npm run dev`
- Typecheck: `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`)
- Lint: `npm run lint` (`eslint`)
- Build: `npm run build` (`npx intlayer build && next build`)
- ALWAYS run `npm run typecheck` before concluding any edit. Zero TypeScript errors allowed.

## Architectural Rules
- File Size Limit: Keep components modular and strictly under 120 lines. Decompose large sections into clean atomic UI components.
- App Router Pages: `src/app/[locale]/`
- Reusable UI Components: `src/components/`
- Content Dictionaries: `src/app/[locale]/**/*.content.ts` (Intlayer format)
- Services / Config: `src/services/` & `src/lib/`

## Visual Polish & Anti-AI-Slop Directives
- Canvas: `#F4F6F9` (never raw white or muddy dark background).
- Surface / Cards: Pure white `#FFFFFF` with soft borders (`border-slate-200/80`) and subtle shadows (`shadow-xs` / `shadow-sm`).
- Interactivity: Every clickable element (buttons, links, triggers, cards) MUST have `cursor-pointer`.
- Micro-interactions: Smooth transitions (`transition-all duration-150 ease-in-out`) on hover and focus.
- Anti-Squish Containers: Strict aspect ratios and overflow boundaries; never let banners, cards, or logos squash or stretch vertically.

## Operational Guardrails
1. Systematic Debugging: Identify root cause with evidence before patching.
2. Strict Verification: Run typecheck before reporting complete.
3. Git Safety: No `git push --force` or `git reset --hard`.
4. Token Optimization: Concise responses, link to files, avoid re-printing unchanged code.
